{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06G9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$1$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathfrak{m}_A$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathbf{N} = \\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\underline{U}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(U, -): \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\underline{U}$", "MATH_0010": "$h_U(-) = \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(-, U)$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Lambda \\to k$", "MATH_0013": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0015": "$k' \\subset k$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0017": "$k' = \\Lambda/\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0018": "$k/k'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remarks-cofibered-groupoids}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{item-definition-yoneda}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{equation-k-prime}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fc186df1bb01103ed744db5789fb5725a3439700945e241a2b5b1f8805c2b77b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7aef1b0670ecd1b4cb4ca25162b5b96c37258605e4885b5e7f7752757f8b0617", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA ring is commutative with <MATH_0001>. The  maximal ideal of a local ring <MATH_0002>\nis denoted by <MATH_0003>. The set of positive integers is denoted\nby <MATH_0004>. If <MATH_0005> is an object of a\ncategory <MATH_0006>, we denote by <MATH_0007>\nthe functor\n<MATH_0008>, see\nRemarks <REF_0001> (<REF_0002>).\nWarning: this may conflict with the notation in other chapters where we\nsometimes use <MATH_0009> to denote <MATH_0010>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThroughout this chapter <MATH_0011> is a Noetherian ring and\n<MATH_0012> is a finite ring map from <MATH_0013> to a field.\nThe kernel of this map is denoted <MATH_0014> and the\nimage <MATH_0015>. It turns out that <MATH_0016> is\na maximal ideal, <MATH_0017> is a field, and\nthe extension <MATH_0018> is finite. See discussion surrounding\n(<REF_0003>).\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5024b2a8239f57b4fba8d21fe28e2ca046b48e38be29b5f4471efec473a50514", "unit_id": "tag:06G9:prose-0001"}
